WEBVTT

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:07.580
One of the most important things to
understand about AI is that an answer can

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.440
sound convincing and still be wrong. It
can be written beautifully.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.560
It can sound certain. It can even include
a reference that appears legitimate.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.640
None of those things, by themselves,
establish that the answer is correct.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.340
AI can misunderstand your question,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.420
leave out important context,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.120
or produce information that is inaccurate
or outdated.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.820
Sometimes it may supply a detail or source
that does not exist.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.980
That is why your judgment belongs in the
process.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.400
When an answer matters, ask: What supports
this? Can I check the source?

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.960
Does the information apply to my
situation?

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.800
Asking AI to check itself can be helpful,
but it is not independent verification.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.860
Follow the reference. Read the original
information.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.700
Consult the appropriate professional when
the decision calls for it. There is

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.560
another consideration: privacy. Before
sharing a document or personal

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.740
detail, think about what the service
actually needs.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.040
Remove unnecessary identifying
information.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.740
Review the service’s privacy settings and
policies.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.020
You can often get useful help by
describing a situation without revealing

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:25.900
everything about yourself or someone else.
Also, pay attention to

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.200
how the answer influences you. AI may
overlook another perspective.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.160
It may agree with an assumption that
deserves to be questioned.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.500
Ask it to explain the limitations,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.260
examine alternatives,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.380
and identify what remains uncertain.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:46.340
And remember: a warm, responsive
conversation does not guarantee

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.220
understanding or accuracy.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.720
Use AI to help you prepare,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.540
explore, organize, and think through
possibilities.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.800
Keep responsibility for your decisions
with you. At ACA,

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.440
we express this in five words:

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.300
AI assists. Humans verify.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.120
Those words become valuable when we put
them into practice.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.740
Thank you for joining us. We look forward
to learning with you.

